{
  "about": "Malayalam glossary for drharshmaheshwari.com. Every Malayalam translation must use these terms: tests/i18n.test.mjs checks that when an English text contains a term, its Malayalam has one of the accepted forms (substring match, so most forms are stems that every inflection contains: Malayalam joins case endings to the word, and a final chillu letter changes when an ending is added, e.g. കൊളസ്ട്രോൾ / കൊളസ്ട്രോളിന്റെ). Modern atomic chillu letters (ൻ ർ ൽ ൾ ൺ) are used throughout. Change a term here, then retranslate what uses it. docs/translation.md has the rules.",
  "register": "Everyday Malayalam that a family in Kochi or Thiruvananthapuram would read easily, like a good health column in a Malayalam newspaper, not heavy Sanskritised Malayalam. Common English health words that people say in Malayalam stay as they are said (BMI, ബ്ലഡ് ഷുഗർ, കൊളസ്ട്രോൾ, ഫാറ്റി ലിവർ, ഡോക്ടർ). Short sentences. Numbers in 0-9, never Malayalam digits. Units as in English (cm, kg). Modern Unicode chillu letters.",
